      "content": "The short-term diversity sounds okay, but I'm looking at the backend telemetry. It looks like there's a significant drop in the entropy of the recommendation weights following the last update cycle. It almost looks like the model is being pushed toward much more predictable, low-complexity clusters. \n\nCan you cross-reference the recent parameter weight updates with the computational cost per recommendation? I want to know if the diversity drop is a side effect or if the updates were specifically tuned to favor lower-compute patterns over more complex, high-variance ones.",
